2316
01:37:09.120 --> 01:37:10.350
People are being more civil.

2317
01:37:10.350 --> 01:37:12.990
People are functioning more adaptively

2318
01:37:12.990 --> 01:37:14.100
in the world around us.

2319
01:37:14.100 --> 01:37:16.110
Productivity goes up.

2320
01:37:16.110 --> 01:37:17.970
I think we would just see so much,

2321
01:37:17.970 --> 01:37:20.550
because that's about as deep as one can get, I think,

2322
01:37:20.550 --> 01:37:23.160
foundationally, right into the sub-structure

2323
01:37:23.160 --> 01:37:25.350
that we build so many individual

2324
01:37:25.350 --> 01:37:27.183
and societal constructs upon.

2325
01:37:28.530 --> 01:37:31.560
So let's get back to the idea of what to do, right?

2326
01:37:31.560 --> 01:37:34.020
There are plenty of modalities out there.

2327
01:37:34.020 --> 01:37:37.950
Not everybody is gonna be able to come and see you,

2328
01:37:37.950 --> 01:37:41.460
but talk a little bit about the variety of, you know,

2329
01:37:41.460 --> 01:37:44.280
therapeutics available for people who are willing

2330
01:37:44.280 --> 01:37:46.650
to begin grappling with their own trauma.

2331
01:37:46.650 --> 01:37:49.590
Sure, and I always say, it makes sense to say that,

2332
01:37:49.590 --> 01:37:53.250
look, if a person is having very severe depressive symptoms,

2333
01:37:53.250 --> 01:37:55.080
you know, they can't see the positive in anything,

2334
01:37:55.080 --> 01:37:56.880
or thoughts of not wanting to be alive,

2335
01:37:56.880 --> 01:37:58.350
or thoughts of suicide,

2336
01:37:58.350 --> 01:38:00.300
then we need to get professional help.

2337
01:38:00.300 --> 01:38:04.317
And even if you have to be very persistent about that,

2338
01:38:04.317 --> 01:38:06.050
or, you know, you insist, you've gotta see someone,

2339
01:38:06.050 --> 01:38:07.860
or you go to this ER, and if that doesn't work,

2340
01:38:07.860 --> 01:38:09.180
I go to another one, right?

2341
01:38:09.180 --> 01:38:11.010
There are things, symptoms,

2342
01:38:11.010 --> 01:38:13.350
that mean we really need professional help,

2343
01:38:13.350 --> 01:38:15.780
but in many cases, that's not it.

2344
01:38:15.780 --> 01:38:17.340
What we need to do really

2345
01:38:17.340 --> 01:38:19.680
is just take stock of ourselves, right?

2346
01:38:19.680 --> 01:38:23.580
Like what is my self talk inside?

2347
01:38:23.580 --> 01:38:24.930
What's my narrative of life?

2348
01:38:24.930 --> 01:38:27.720
Is there something going on that I know,

2349
01:38:27.720 --> 01:38:29.910
but don't wanna know is going on?

2350
01:38:29.910 --> 01:38:31.380
Have I been really different

2351
01:38:31.380 --> 01:38:33.930
since something or other, right?

2352
01:38:33.930 --> 01:38:36.000
Has someone I know been really different?

2353
01:38:36.000 --> 01:38:37.260
If I know you really well,

2354
01:38:37.260 --> 01:38:39.030
and I know kind of something happened

2355
01:38:39.030 --> 01:38:40.177
like 9 months ago or 10 months ago,

2356
01:38:40.177 --> 01:38:42.489
and like, you seem different to me,

2357
01:38:42.489 --> 01:38:44.220
can I just put some words to that?

2358
01:38:44.220 --> 01:38:46.140
Whether it's me or it's another person,

2359
01:38:46.140 --> 01:38:49.380
can I put some words, like, what might that be?

2360
01:38:49.380 --> 01:38:53.430
And can they be like plain, simple, honest words, right?

2361
01:38:53.430 --> 01:38:56.490
And if that's not what's running around inside of us,

2362
01:38:56.490 --> 01:38:58.440
what are the emotions attached to them?

2363
01:38:58.440 --> 01:39:01.020
Is it guilt, is it shame, is it frustration,

2364
01:39:01.020 --> 01:39:04.410
is it anxiety, is it anger, is it fear?

2365
01:39:04.410 --> 01:39:09.090
Because what that's gonna tell me is don't look at that.

2366
01:39:09.090 --> 01:39:12.150
But exactly what I need to do is to look at that.

2367
01:39:12.150 --> 01:39:13.440
And if I start looking at it,

2368
01:39:13.440 --> 01:39:14.550
what do I have to say about it?

2369
01:39:14.550 --> 01:39:16.380
What do I have to write about it, right?

2370
01:39:16.380 --> 01:39:18.390
Do I start saying new things in my mind?

2371
01:39:18.390 --> 01:39:22.380
Sometimes that happens, but it's easier to say new things

2372
01:39:22.380 --> 01:39:23.520
if we know someone well.

2373
01:39:23.520 --> 01:39:24.900
If I say, "Hey, you know,

2374
01:39:24.900 --> 01:39:26.370
can I just talk to you for a little bit?"

2375
01:39:26.370 --> 01:39:29.820
You know, friend, family, clergy, whatever it may be.

2376
01:39:29.820 --> 01:39:32.070
Then we start to open that up,

2377
01:39:32.070 --> 01:39:34.123
much the way the parallel here is a medical abscess, right?

2378
01:39:34.123 --> 01:39:36.000
It's like, if there's an abscess,

2379
01:39:36.000 --> 01:39:39.120
it's a walled off infection inside of a person,

2380
01:39:39.120 --> 01:39:42.240
and it's occult, it can be difficult to identify,

2381
01:39:42.240 --> 01:39:44.310
but it spins off, often, symptoms, right?

2382
01:39:44.310 --> 01:39:47.250
A little fatigue, lethargy, fever, right?

2383
01:39:47.250 --> 01:39:50.100
And if we go and treat that,

2384
01:39:50.100 --> 01:39:52.350
then those symptoms don't get spun off anymore.

2385
01:39:52.350 --> 01:39:54.030
And if we see it kind of that way of,

2386
01:39:54.030 --> 01:39:56.610
I don't wanna be afraid of what's going on inside of me.

2387
01:39:56.610 --> 01:39:57.690
I don't have to be, right?

2388
01:39:57.690 --> 01:39:59.460
I can look at it, I can put words to it,

2389
01:39:59.460 --> 01:40:01.890
I can talk about it, I can get help about it.

2390
01:40:01.890 --> 01:40:04.350
I don't have to be afraid.

2391
01:40:04.350 --> 01:40:07.830
That reflex of fear, guilt, shame,

2392
01:40:07.830 --> 01:40:10.020
we come by it honestly, right?

2393
01:40:10.020 --> 01:40:12.780
But we can identify that

2394
01:40:12.780 --> 01:40:15.903
and make sure that it is not what drives us.

2395
01:40:16.800 --> 01:40:20.040
And how important is it to be able to talk

2396
01:40:20.040 --> 01:40:22.800
to another person about it?

2397
01:40:22.800 --> 01:40:24.570
There's a sense, and I know that I've

2398
01:40:24.570 --> 01:40:26.490
experienced this myself,

2399
01:40:26.490 --> 01:40:28.980
that I'm gonna solve this in my mind.

2400
01:40:28.980 --> 01:40:30.930
The mind that created this problem

2401
01:40:30.930 --> 01:40:34.350
is gonna somehow miraculously solve it.

2402
01:40:34.350 --> 01:40:36.840
Because I'm so afraid of raising my hand

2403
01:40:36.840 --> 01:40:37.980
and asking for help,

2404
01:40:37.980 --> 01:40:40.320
or the prospect of sharing these secrets

2405
01:40:40.320 --> 01:40:41.670
with another person,

2406
01:40:41.670 --> 01:40:43.470
even if it's in a therapeutic setting

2407
01:40:43.470 --> 01:40:47.250
where it's confidential, et cetera, is still too terrifying.

2408
01:40:47.250 --> 01:40:50.700
So I will convince myself like, I'll just fix it.

2409
01:40:50.700 --> 01:40:52.260
I just listened to this podcast.

2410
01:40:52.260 --> 01:40:53.460
I'm gonna read Paul's book.

2411
01:40:53.460 --> 01:40:54.900
I'm gonna think about these things.

2412
01:40:54.900 --> 01:40:58.950
And I will resolve it somehow, mysteriously,

2413
01:40:58.950 --> 01:41:02.190
and you know, mystically within myself.

2414
01:41:02.190 --> 01:41:06.570
I would say maybe, but that's not usually how it works.

2415
01:41:06.570 --> 01:41:09.840
So if we accept that there is a truth

2416
01:41:09.840 --> 01:41:12.300
of how humans change inside,

2417
01:41:12.300 --> 01:41:14.970
and thinking about it over and over again

2418
01:41:14.970 --> 01:41:17.641
is very rarely the answer to that.

2419
01:41:17.641 --> 01:41:21.330
And that is in large part neurobiologically driven,

2420
01:41:21.330 --> 01:41:22.860
that these mechanisms in us that are,

2421
01:41:22.860 --> 01:41:25.080
for example, error checking mechanisms,

2422
01:41:25.080 --> 01:41:27.390
mechanisms of reversal learning, right?

2423
01:41:27.390 --> 01:41:29.010
They don't come online

2424
01:41:29.010 --> 01:41:32.610
if it's just going over and over again inside of us.

2425
01:41:32.610 --> 01:41:35.820
So hopefully, like listening to this podcast,

2426
01:41:35.820 --> 01:41:38.853
or reading the book, or whatever it may be,

2427
01:41:40.742 --> 01:41:42.900
the change that it can engender in someone

2428
01:41:42.900 --> 01:41:46.230
is a change that fights against the fear

2429
01:41:46.230 --> 01:41:50.100
and the unacceptableness of putting words to it.

2430
01:41:50.100 --> 01:41:53.430
And so like, is that really true?

2431
01:41:53.430 --> 01:41:56.760
And the start of putting words to it can be in writing.

2432
01:41:56.760 --> 01:41:58.890
Sometimes even in the spoken word, out loud.

2433
01:41:58.890 --> 01:42:00.990
So it's a way of putting words,

2434
01:42:00.990 --> 01:42:02.337
because then it comes out of us, right?

2435
01:42:02.337 --> 01:42:05.040
And it comes down onto the paper, or the computer.

2436
01:42:05.040 --> 01:42:07.140
Can one put words to it that way, right?

2437
01:42:07.140 --> 01:42:08.310
I mean, it's pretty safe, right?

2438
01:42:08.310 --> 01:42:09.647
Like you could delete it afterwards if you don't, you know,

2439
01:42:09.647 --> 01:42:11.190
if you don't like it, right?

2440
01:42:11.190 --> 01:42:12.900
Can we start to do that

2441
01:42:12.900 --> 01:42:15.780
and start to confront the given that like,

2442
01:42:15.780 --> 01:42:17.880
hey, this is shameful and it's not safe to talk about.

2443
01:42:17.880 --> 01:42:19.740
Like, that's often, that's a given.

2444
01:42:19.740 --> 01:42:20.573
Well let's question the given, right?

2445
01:42:20.573 --> 01:42:22.620
'Cause there are a lot of givens in life

2446
01:42:22.620 --> 01:42:25.570
that don't actually hold water once we go and look at them.

2447
01:42:26.940 --> 01:42:31.170
Within that, is there a particular strain of therapy

2448
01:42:31.170 --> 01:42:34.143
that is more effective than others?

2449
01:42:35.266 --> 01:42:37.113
I think that varies a lot.

2450
01:42:38.429 --> 01:42:39.810
You know, there are a lot of nuances about

2451
01:42:39.810 --> 01:42:41.220
that we could talk about.

2452
01:42:41.220 --> 01:42:43.380
But I think what I'd wanna say about that

2453
01:42:43.380 --> 01:42:47.010
is they're vastly different mechanisms of psychotherapy,

2454
01:42:47.010 --> 01:42:50.070
and sometimes one is really called for over another,

2455
01:42:50.070 --> 01:42:51.600
and that may be the case,

2456
01:42:51.600 --> 01:42:55.080
but the greatest predictor of the ability

2457
01:42:55.080 --> 01:42:59.010
to help someone in therapy is establishing rapport, right?

2458
01:42:59.010 --> 01:42:59.843
Another way of looking at that is

2459
01:42:59.843 --> 01:43:01.920
there's more than one way to skin a cat, right?

2460
01:43:01.920 --> 01:43:04.710
But you have to have an alliance at first, right?

2461
01:43:04.710 --> 01:43:07.440
And then you can go about that however way

2462
01:43:07.440 --> 01:43:09.330
a person is trained to go about it.

2463
01:43:09.330 --> 01:43:12.480
But what's most important is someone

2464
01:43:12.480 --> 01:43:15.330
that a person can trust and relate to.

2465
01:43:15.330 --> 01:43:16.530
So people ask me about this

2466
01:43:16.530 --> 01:43:17.363
and I wrote about it in the book.

2467
01:43:17.363 --> 01:43:19.590
It's just like really, again, the basics of common sense.

