But we have to look at, what are we treating with them?

2503
01:44:44.910 --> 01:44:46.770
And what are they in the service of?

2504
01:44:46.770 --> 01:44:50.970
Like, meaning like SSRIs don't fix,

2505
01:44:50.970 --> 01:44:53.130
quote, unquote, "trauma," right?

2506
01:44:53.130 --> 01:44:58.130
But sometimes SSRIs can improve distress tolerance,

2507
01:44:58.440 --> 01:45:00.300
decrease anxiety a little bit,

2508
01:45:00.300 --> 01:45:01.830
and make it easier thereby

2509
01:45:01.830 --> 01:45:04.680
for the person to confront the trauma, right?

2510
01:45:04.680 --> 01:45:07.620
Same thing if you're not sleeping and you're ruminative.

2511
01:45:07.620 --> 01:45:09.930
I mean, if we don't get good restorative sleep,

2512
01:45:09.930 --> 01:45:11.670
we're not solving way out of a paper bag.

2513
01:45:11.670 --> 01:45:14.040
I mean, that's just true of us as human beings, right?

2514
01:45:14.040 --> 01:45:15.990
So if that's going on,

2515
01:45:15.990 --> 01:45:17.910
is there a medicine we can bring to bear

2516
01:45:17.910 --> 01:45:19.290
so that person can sleep

2517
01:45:19.290 --> 01:45:21.000
and they can be at their best again?

2518
01:45:21.000 --> 01:45:22.890
And they can face this from that perspective.

2519
01:45:22.890 --> 01:45:25.770
So there are a lot of ways that medicines can help

2520
01:45:25.770 --> 01:45:27.720
in a lot of circumstances,

2521
01:45:27.720 --> 01:45:32.670
but we cannot mistake them for answers to the problems.

2522
01:45:32.670 --> 01:45:34.590
And they should be prescribed

2523
01:45:34.590 --> 01:45:35.850
with a very clear understanding

2524
01:45:35.850 --> 01:45:37.350
of what are they in the service of.

2525
01:45:37.350 --> 01:45:39.210
So if you come and see me and we're talking about trauma

2526
01:45:39.210 --> 01:45:40.620
and I think, hey, look,

2527
01:45:40.620 --> 01:45:43.650
you could really benefit from an anti-ruminative at bedtime,

2528
01:45:43.650 --> 01:45:45.930
and you could really benefit from an anti-anxiety medicine

2529
01:45:45.930 --> 01:45:47.520
because you're having seven panic attacks a day,

2530
01:45:47.520 --> 01:45:50.760
and it's so hard to live and solve one's problems then,

2531
01:45:50.760 --> 01:45:52.740
then I should talk to you about that.

2532
01:45:52.740 --> 01:45:54.270
Like here's what's going on.

2533
01:45:54.270 --> 01:45:56.730
Here's what we would try and treat with these medicines.

2534
01:45:56.730 --> 01:45:58.560
Here's the risks and benefits and side effects.

2535
01:45:58.560 --> 01:46:02.400
And here's why they're temporary in nature, we expect,

2536
01:46:02.400 --> 01:46:05.430
in the service of helping you do what you need to do

2537
01:46:05.430 --> 01:46:06.900
so that you don't need them anymore.

2538
01:46:06.900 --> 01:46:11.310
Right, so they're not specific to treating the trauma.

2539
01:46:11.310 --> 01:46:13.830
They're about getting you into a place

2540
01:46:13.830 --> 01:46:18.830
where you can be receptive to therapy, right?

2541
01:46:18.960 --> 01:46:20.460
Therapeutic interventions.

2542
01:46:20.460 --> 01:46:23.660
Right, which is really an enaction of common sense

2543
01:46:23.660 --> 01:46:24.750
in the provider of saying,

2544
01:46:24.750 --> 01:46:26.880
hey, if you're coming to me, then I'm gonna say, well,

2545
01:46:26.880 --> 01:46:28.590
I have seven medicines I use for trauma.

2546
01:46:28.590 --> 01:46:29.447
Like, I don't know who you are yet,

2547
01:46:29.447 --> 01:46:30.480
right?
Right.

2548
01:46:30.480 --> 01:46:32.490
So you come and tell me what's going on with you.

2549
01:46:32.490 --> 01:46:34.560
If I see, hey, there's a couple of things going on in you

2550
01:46:34.560 --> 01:46:36.810
that are number one, making you miserable,

2551
01:46:36.810 --> 01:46:38.520
and number two, making it really hard

2552
01:46:38.520 --> 01:46:39.810
to process your trauma,

2553
01:46:39.810 --> 01:46:41.280
well, let's talk about that.

2554
01:46:41.280 --> 01:46:43.710
And let's decide, like, does that sound reasonable to you?

2555
01:46:43.710 --> 01:46:45.360
Like, can I talk about it in a way

2556
01:46:45.360 --> 01:46:47.100
that you can understand well enough?

2557
01:46:47.100 --> 01:46:48.657
If not, I'm not doing a good enough job of it, right?

2558
01:46:48.657 --> 01:46:51.300
And then ultimately it's you who makes that decision.

2559
01:46:51.300 --> 01:46:55.170
Yeah, I'm gonna serve my own cause with this,

2560
01:46:55.170 --> 01:46:56.003
or these medicines,

2561
01:46:56.003 --> 01:46:58.290
but I understand what they can do for me

2562
01:46:58.290 --> 01:46:59.550
and what they can't.

2563
01:46:59.550 --> 01:47:02.700
It's just the common sense use of medicines

2564
01:47:02.700 --> 01:47:04.740
in the service of the greater good,

2565
01:47:04.740 --> 01:47:07.377
instead of medicines as mystery, right?

2566
01:47:07.377 --> 01:47:08.940
And how many people, I mean,

